WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.424 --> 00:00:03.591
(gentle upbeat music)

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.850
- [Narrator] Cannabis, it's
the most frequently used

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.240
illicit substance in the United States

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.513
and arguably, one of
the most controversial.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.320
Cannabis, or marijuana, is a drug

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.980
derived from certain strains

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.033
of the plant cannabis sativa.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.550
The plant's flowers and leaves

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.680
contain chemical compounds
called cannabinoids,

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.803
which produce cannabis's
mind altering effects.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.430
This high is largely
caused by the cannabinoid

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:39.043
called tetrahydrocannabinol, or THC.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:43.580
When THC from cannabis
is ingested or inhaled,

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:47.020
it overwhelms the body's
natural levels of THC

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.323
in the cardiovascular and
central nervous systems.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.700
In the brain, THC attaches to neurons

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.840
that send information via chemicals

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.610
known as neurotransmitters.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.750
The THC decreases the
amount of neurotransmitters

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.630
the neurons produce, thereby decreasing

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.150
the amount of information transmitted.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:10.090
This results in psychoactive effects

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:13.610
such as lack of coordination, memory loss,

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.443
hallucinations, and increased appetite.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.420
Because of some of the
psychoactive effects,

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.790
cannabis had been used
for medicinal purposes

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:24.273
for thousands of years.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.120
Then around the 20th Century,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.920
cannabis became more accessible

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.500
and more widely used for
recreational purposes.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.040
But by the late 1960s, the use

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.550
and possession of cannabis
became illegal in many countries

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.850
due to debate surrounding
the drug's effects.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.320
Opponents state that
the dangers of cannabis

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.110
include inducing heart attacks,
decreasing sperm count,

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:51.963
and stunting brain development,
particularly in teenagers.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.980
Proponents, especially
of medicinal marijuana,

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.800
site benefits including treating seizures,

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.460
relieving chronic pain,
and preventing nausea

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.193
induced by chemotherapy.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:08.120
Because of cannabis's costs and benefits,

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.210
many countries continue to wrestle

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.490
with how to best approach and regulate

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:14.333
the controversial substance.

